erver","feedback_revision":"a44f89137b9cc9e96f49a110","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"no_diagnostic_value"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_bus_scheduling_model_832ce4e9_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"The cyclic bus model has six four-hour intervals (1: midnight–4 AM, …, 6: 8 PM–midnight), $x_i$ buses starting in interval $i$, each running two consecutive intervals, requirements $d=(4,8,10,7,12,4)$ and constraints $x_{i-1}+x_i\\ge d_i$ with $x_0=x_6$. For the schedule $x=(2,6,4,3,9,2)$, how many buses are on the road from 8 PM to midnight?","options":["2","11","4","13"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"064c9f6bca350c84c5c068e4","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_bus_scheduling_model_832ce4e9_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In the bus model $\\min\\sum_i x_i$ s.t. $x_{i-1}+x_i\\ge d_i$ ($x_0=x_6$), the requirements are integers. Why is the restriction $x_i\\in\\mathbb{Z}_{\\ge0}$ still written into the model?","options":["Integer $d_i$ do not prevent a fractional continuous optimum","Integer restrictions lower the minimum number of buses needed","Without them, the coverage constraints would not be linear","Without them, negative numbers of buses could be chosen"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dd662c582e759154bf2b7da4","time_limit":35,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_bus_scheduling_model_832ce4e9_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A cyclic bus model lets $x_i$ buses start an eight-hour shift in four-hour interval $i$ with requirements $d_i$, and minimizes $\\sum_{i=1}^6x_i$ as the number of buses needed. Which assumption makes this sum equal the number of buses?","options":["No bus starts a second shift on the same day","Each interval has the same requirement $d_i$","Each interval is covered by exactly $d_i$ buses","Each bus starts its shift at midnight or noon"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"559bb1937fa8ce84b6e47763","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"}]}}